==Irish==

===Etymology===
From {{term|ag|lang=ga}} + {{term|a|lang=ga}}.

===Contraction===
{{infl|ga|pronoun|sort=a}}

# [[him]], [[her]], [[it]], [[them]]

====Usage notes====
* Used before the verbal noun to indicate third person direct object;
*# Triggers [[lenition]] when meaning [[him]], or [[it]] (if referring to a masculine noun):
*#: '''{{l|ga|tá|Táim}} á {{l|ga|buail|bhualadh}}''' -- ''[[I]] [[be|am]] [[hit|hitting]] '''[[him]]'''''
*#: '''{{l|ga|tá|Táim}} á {{l|ga|ól}}''' -- ''[[I]] [[be|am]] [[drink|drinking]] '''[[it]]'''''
*# Triggers no change (or '''h''' before a vowel) when meaning [[her]], or [[it]] (if referring to a feminine noun):
*#: '''{{l|ga|tá|Táim}} á {{l|ga|buail|bualadh}}''' -- ''[[I]] [[be|am]] [[hit|hitting]] '''[[her]]'''''
*#: '''{{l|ga|tá|Táim}} á {{l|ga|ól|hól}}''' -- ''[[I]] [[be|am]] [[drink|drinking]] '''[[it]]'''''
*# Triggers [[eclipsis]] (including '''n-''' before a vowel) when meaning [[them]]:
*#: '''{{l|ga|tá|Táim}} á {{l|ga|buail|mbualadh}}''' -- ''[[I]] [[be|am]] [[hit|hitting]] '''[[them]]'''''
*#: '''{{l|ga|tá|Táim}} á {{l|ga|ól|n-ól}}''' -- ''[[I]] [[be|am]] [[drink|drinking]] '''[[them]]'''''

====Related terms====
* {{l|ga|a}}
* {{l|ga|ag}}
* {{l|ga|do}}

